; The vocabulary of a patio somebody is about to decide a drainage fall across.
;
; The decision came first and is written down before anything was derived:
; docs/surface-accuracy-gate.md states what the fall has to be known to, and it
; states it in millimetres of standard uncertainty rather than as a feeling about
; whether the survey looks good enough.
;
; Nothing in this file says anything about a surface, and nothing in it says how
; well an afternoon on one base station is known. The first is derived from the
; shots inside a region every time it is asked
; (docs/decisions/0009-derived-values-are-never-written-back.md); the second is
; stated on the derivation, because the observation format carries the precision
; of a shot and not the worth of a setup.
;
; Two pieces of ground of the same shape, ten metres apart, surveyed at the same
; density by two instruments. That is the whole design of the fixture: what
; differs between the answers cannot be the density, because the density is
; identical.
(project
  (label "Patio fall accuracy gate")
  (globalid-namespace "https://example.org/models/patio"))

(namespace control (description "Survey control the measurements are tied to."))
(namespace fix (description "Fix qualities an instrument reports."))
(namespace frame (description "Coordinate frames declared by this model."))
(namespace geom (description "Geometric nodes minted by this model."))
(namespace method (description "How a value was obtained."))
(namespace session (description "Field occupations: one setup, one crew, one afternoon."))
(namespace shot (description "Observation records issued by the field crew."))
(namespace site (description "Semantic nodes minted by this model."))
(namespace survey (description "Claim ids issued by Acme Surveys."))

(predicate position
  (unit m)
  (shape coordinate)
  (dimension 3)
  (description "The location of a vertex in its frame."))

(frame frame:site (label "Site survey grid") (unit m))

(type Patio
  (kind Space)
  (geometry area)
  (description "Paved ground laid to a fall."))

(tolerance boundary-closure
  (value 0.005 m)
  (description "How far a loop may fail to close, how far out of one plane its corners may lie, and how close two corners are one corner."))

(route everything
  (file "entities/patio.dfc")
  (description "One file, which is all a fixture this size needs."))
